From ffc83be90727a00bc5ce9732da66be835ace015d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alessio Igor Bogani <alessio.bogani@elettra.eu>
Date: Mon, 4 May 2026 14:10:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Fix termios build when <sys/ioctl.h> uses struct termio
 without defining it

On Linux/glibc, <bits/ioctls.h> (pulled in by <sys/ioctl.h>) expands the
TCGETA/TCSETA/TCSETAF/TCSETAW ioctl macros to _IOR('t', N, struct termio)
but does not itself include the header that defines struct termio. On
toolchains where <termio.h> is not implicitly visible (e.g. some
PowerPC SPE cross sysroots), this caused:

    invalid application of 'sizeof' to incomplete type 'struct termio'

Probe for <termio.h> in configure and include it from Modules/termios.c
before <sys/ioctl.h> so the struct is complete when the ioctl macros are
expanded. The existing QNX-specific <sys/termio.h> path is left intact.
---

